Recoil [
    Title: "Loos editor size"
    Description: {
        The one place Loos's editor size is written down.

        It used to be two: the editor declared it, and made
        `*_editor_attach` REFUSE any other size, while the plug-in
        descriptor stated it again as bare literals under a comment saying
        the two must match. Nothing checked that they did, and a mismatch is
        not a diagnostic -- the host sizes its window from the descriptor,
        the attach refuses that size, and the player gets a silent black
        rectangle.

        A module of two constants rather than an import of the editor
        itself: importing the editor would compile its whole body into the
        descriptor's translation unit as well as its own, and every function
        in it would then be defined twice at link time. Constants emit as
        `static const`, so a module carrying nothing else can be imported
        anywhere it is needed.
    }
    Type: module
    Module: examples/pokuston/loos/editor-size
    Exports: [LOOS-EDITOR-WIDTH LOOS-EDITOR-HEIGHT]
]

; Shorter than it was. The filter envelope's row of four went with the second
; ADSR it belonged to, and nothing was moved in to fill the space: the facade
; getting simpler as the interior gets richer is the point of the instrument,
; not an accident of the edit.
LOOS-EDITOR-WIDTH: make i32! 760
LOOS-EDITOR-HEIGHT: make i32! 576
